<title>MALAYSIA: Kuala Lumpur power seen restored around 1200 GMT.</title>
<headline>Kuala Lumpur power seen restored around 1200 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian state power utility Tenaga Nasional Bhd said electricity supply should be restored to Kuala Lumpur's central business area by around 8.0 p.m. local (1200 GMT) on Tuesday after an earlier outage.</p>
<p>&quot;We think it'll be back after 8 p.m.,&quot; a spokeswoman for Tenaga told Reuters.</p>
<p>Power had already been restored to some areas by 1030 GMT, Reuters office in the capital reported.</p>
